<p>The web application serves this dashboard, the client API (<code>/v1</code>), the public API documentation (<code>/docs/api</code>), the tracking links (<code>/t/…</code>) and the re-permission pages (<code>/p/…</code>).
It writes work into the database for the background workers and never sends mail or webhooks itself.</p>
<p>The tracking checks request the open pixel and a click link with a random token, exactly as a stranger would: an unknown token is answered like any other, and nothing is recorded.</p>
